{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791880249,"nonce":"PUZm2FXeD7qkGZEvmbKkJeTfpvA=","title":"Expose stencil-capable shared scene targets for custom passes","message":"ChimpMonk AnimationInspectorSnapshot with native Ranger fails before its first 2D capture: Clipping requires a render target opened with stencil=true. Ranger uses clipped irises and eyelids. ScenePainter hardcodes Depth24plus and ScenePassFrame therefore cannot host the existing AtlasRenderer stencil passes.\n\nReproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/scripts/editor.sh --animation-snapshot. The document checks pass for both formats, but the 2D scene renderer needs stencil attachment support.\n\nPrepared opt-in patch: /tmp/chimpmonk-ashui-stencil.patch. Under -D ashui_scene_stencil, choose Depth24plusStencil8 for the shared scene and glow targets, clear stencil to zero and discard it after both render passes. Default clients retain Depth24plus. ChimpMonk GameLayer detects the frame depth format and advertises hasStencil only for actual stencil formats.\n\nA temporary source overlay of this patch passes all AnimationInspectorSnapshot scenarios in both themes, native 2D and glTF 3D, including the clipped eyes, layer application, invalid edits, preview lock and compact layouts. Reviewed screenshots at /tmp/chimpmonk-animation-tools-stencil. Approval to change the sibling dependency is pending under handoff/spec.md section 10; do not silently disable atlas clipping or introduce a second model loader.","files":null}]}